{"availability":"available","full":"pry/pry","name":"pry","description":"A runtime developer console and IRB alternative with powerful introspection capabilities.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Ruby","stars":6839,"forks":609,"created":"2010-12-07T08:10:47Z","updated":"2026-09-27T21:50:52Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"http://pry.github.io","topics":["console","debugger","introspection","irb","pry","reflection","ruby","runtime"],"demo":"http://pry.github.io/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:40.513Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:40.513Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:40.513Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:36:40.513Z","stars":6839,"forks":609}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["© Kyrylo Silin (kyrylosilin) 2010 (Maintainer)","Pry is a runtime developer console and IRB alternative with powerful introspection capabilities. Pry aims to be more than an IRB replacement. It is an attempt to bring REPL driven programming to the Ruby language.","Pry is fairly flexible and allows significant user customization. It is trivial to read from any object that has a readline method and write to any object that has a puts method. Many other aspects of Pry are also configurable, making it a good choice for implementing custom shells."],"features":["YARD API documentation","Source code browsing (including core C source with the pry-doc gem)","Documentation browsing","Command shell integration (start editors, run git, and rake from within Pry)","Navigation around state (cd, ls and friends)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pry/pry/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"0074e07c7c3bbcee2bcdd4109b5a34df63b8b65671c425fd1ee3cab551c0994b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:40.669Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:40.669Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"© Kyrylo Silin (kyrylosilin) 2010 (Maintainer)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pry/pry/blob/master/READM